; recordrespawn.eval - a type Save and a type Rename rebuild the live level
; from its records and keep everything the editor and play did to it, and an
; undo brings back no monster the editor erased (code-review C311). Judged by
; tools/EditorTest.py phase 32, on a scratch copy of dungeon-demo; monsters are
; frozen throughout, so each stays on the square it is looked for on.
;
; On the active level the LIVE lists were the truth for monsters and props: a
; placement added only an instance and an erase left the record behind. Both
; the type editor's Save (every category with a cached kind - the monster's
; here) and a Rename rebuilt the level from those records, so:
; 1. UNDO. The coward (12,1, an authored record) erased, a barrel placed, the
;    barrel undone: the restore respawned from the records, coward included.
; 2. WHAT A SAVE AND A RENAME MUST KEEP, staged first: a skeleton and a crate
;    the editor placed (no record), a door placed and opened, a potion dropped,
;    the authored skeleton at 12,6 killed, the archer made a sentry in its
;    inspector. The skeleton type is then saved with its hp raised from 16 to
;    20, and renamed to `bones` and back. Each used to drop the placed skeleton
;    and crate, raise the dead, bring the coward back, shut the door, lose the
;    potion and the archer's archetype. `opendoor` reads the door by turning
;    it: `shut` means it was still open. THE CONTROL that the Save rebuilt
;    anything at all: the placed skeleton, untouched, is respawned from the
;    kind read afresh, so it reads hp 20 after it - with no respawn, every
;    check of what was kept would pass on nothing done.
; 3. A DELETE SEES WHAT THE EDITOR PLACED. A lurker - a type no level and no
;    catalog names - placed by the editor had no record, and the delete counted
;    records: the type went from under it, and the save wrote a monster of a
;    type that no longer existed. Now it is refused.
; 4. THE SAVE that follows writes the placed skeleton and the sentry, and no
;    coward - and the lurker, placed after the inspector's Save (which writes
;    the level too), so only this save can have written it.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11
freeze on
editor
echo --- start ---
monsters
editor erase 12 1
editor place decorations barrel 16 16
breakables
undo
echo --- undone ---
monsters
breakables
editor place monsters skeleton 16 18
editor place decorations crate 18 18
editor drag walls wall_marble 1 5 3 5
editor place doors wooden_door 2 5
opendoor 2 5
tp 14 12
face s
drop potion_health 14 13
tp 12 5
face s
effect bleed ahead 999 2
step 1
editor inspect 25 7
editor inspector archetype sentry
editor inspector save
echo --- staged ---
monsters
breakables
flooritems 14 13
typeset monsters skeleton hp 20
echo --- type saved ---
monsters
breakables
flooritems 14 13
editor inspect 25 7
editor inspector
editor inspect off
opendoor 2 5
opendoor 2 5
typeset rename monsters skeleton bones
echo --- renamed ---
monsters
breakables
flooritems 14 13
editor inspect 25 7
editor inspector
editor inspect off
opendoor 2 5
opendoor 2 5
typeset rename monsters bones skeleton
echo --- renamed back ---
monsters
typerefs monsters skel_lurker
editor place monsters skel_lurker 20 20
expect-refuse typeset delete monsters skel_lurker
echo --- delete refused ---
typerefs monsters skel_lurker
savemap
echo --- end ---
